From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AML: start on a mode whose 1000/1001 rate is not listed

The resolution list carries a 1000/1001 twin only for 24, 30 and 60 Hz,
and the desktop resolution is taken from the list entry that matches the
current mode exactly. A Kodi that died in frame-sequential 3D at 23.976
fps leaves the output at 1080p 119.88 Hz, which nothing in the list
matches: the desktop resolution kept its empty default, the mode switch
to it failed, and every restart exited with "Unable to create GUI" until
a reboot.

The current mode now takes the listed entry of the same size whose rate
rounds the same when there is no exact one, so Kodi starts at its twin
(120 Hz) and the cleanup after a Kodi that died in 3D can run.

The twin rule did not cover 1080p165: its VESA timing is not in the list
(only with /flash/vesa.enable), so a Kodi left on it found neither the mode
nor a twin of equal rounded rate and could not create its window. When there
is no exact entry and no twin, the desktop now takes the listed mode of the
same size and flags at the nearest rate, else the sink's preferred mode, else
the first listed one: the desktop resolution never stays without a mode.

The cleanup after a Kodi that died in 3D only looked at game VRR, so one that
died at a film rate without VRR (vrr_mode none), or after a failed entry,
left ALLM on, the eyes swapped, the video layer's 3D type and the 3D base
mode behind. Entering 3D now records, in special://temp/fs3d-state, ALLM as
it was and the mode the output was on; leaving deletes the record. On its
first display refresh Kodi clears the video layer's 3D type and the eye swap
whatever it finds (the kernel keeps the 3D type across a decoder reset, since
a pause or a seek needs it, so nothing else clears it after a Kodi died), and
takes the rest of 3D down if the record is there, the sink is in game VRR, or
fa_swap_eyes was set: VRR off and ALLM back to the recorded value (0 without
a record, since ALLM on next to the rest of 3D was ours). The record survives a reboot, as the
output mode does. If the output is on the 3D base mode (1080p120 or
1080p165), the desktop resolution is taken from the recorded mode rather
than from the output, so Kodi switches back to it and the box no longer
keeps, and boots at, 1080p120/165. The base mode alone, with nothing else
of 3D left, is taken for a desktop someone chose and only the 3D state is
cleared.

If the record cannot be written, a warning says so; 3D is entered as before.

The record is deleted only once the output is off the 3D base mode: after
the switch back succeeds when 3D is left or an entry fails, and after the
recovered desktop has been set on the next start. Leaving 3D when Kodi exits
changes no mode, so it keeps the record, and the next start recovers the
desktop; a Kodi exit or reboot in 3D, or a failed switch back, no longer
leaves the GUI booting at 1080p120/165.

If the recorded mode is no longer listed (another sink), the desktop is the
sink's preferred mode, else the nearest mode of the current size that is not
a 3D base, so the output still leaves 1080p120/165 and the record goes.

Entering 3D keeps an existing record when the output is already on the 3D
base mode (a switch back failed, or a recovered record is pending) instead
of overwriting the desktop it names with the base mode. A record kept after
a failed switch back is marked pending, so it is deleted once a later switch
leaves the base mode in the same session.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/AMLDisplay.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/AMLDisplay.cpp
index bc646f2d6a..d73d414a2b 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/AMLDisplay.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/AMLDisplay.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <cmath>
 #include <cstdlib>
 #include <fcntl.h>
+#include <fstream>
 #include <sys/ioctl.h>
 #include <amcodec/codec.h>
 
@@ -1154,20 +1155,91 @@ void CAMLDisplay::aml_refresh_display_caps()
     m_support_fs3d = support_fs3d;
   }
 
-  // A Kodi that died in 3D left the sink in game VRR, and the video layer
-  // alternating the eyes. Only on the first refresh, before this Kodi has
-  // entered 3D itself: a hotplug refresh while entering (game VRR set, not
-  // yet marked active) would take its own 3D down.
+  // A Kodi that died in 3D left the sink in game VRR (or ALLM alone, at a film
+  // rate without VRR), the video layer alternating the eyes, and the output on
+  // the 3D base mode. Only on the first refresh, before this Kodi has entered 3D
+  // itself: a hotplug refresh while entering (game VRR set, not yet marked
+  // active) would take its own 3D down.
   const bool first_refresh = !m_fs3d_recovery_checked.exchange(true);
-  if (first_refresh && !m_fs3d_active &&
-      StringUtils::StartsWith(
-          CSysfsPath("/sys/class/amhdmitx/amhdmitx0/vrr_mode").Get<std::string>().value_or(""),
-          "game"))
+  if (first_refresh && !m_fs3d_active)
+    fs3d_recover();
+}
+
+namespace
+{
+// what entering HFR VRR changed, kept until it is left: a Kodi that dies in 3D
+// leaves it for the next one, across a reboot too (the output mode is kept)
+constexpr const char* FS3D_STATE = "special://temp/fs3d-state";
+} // unnamed namespace
+
+void CAMLDisplay::fs3d_state_save(const std::string& allm, const RESOLUTION_INFO& before)
+{
+  const std::string path = CSpecialProtocol::TranslatePath(FS3D_STATE);
+  std::ofstream state(path, std::ios::trunc);
+  state << allm << '\n' << before.strId << '\n' << before.fRefreshRate << '\n';
+  state.close();
+  if (!state)
+    CLog::Log(LOGWARNING, "CAMLDisplay::{} - could not write {}: after a crash in 3D the "
+              "ALLM and desktop mode from before cannot be restored", __FUNCTION__, path);
+}
+
+void CAMLDisplay::fs3d_state_clear()
+{
+  std::remove(CSpecialProtocol::TranslatePath(FS3D_STATE).c_str());
+}
+
+void CAMLDisplay::fs3d_recover()
+{
+  std::string allm;
+  std::string modeId;
+  float modeRate = 0.0f;
+  std::ifstream state(CSpecialProtocol::TranslatePath(FS3D_STATE));
+  const bool saved = static_cast<bool>(state);
+  if (saved)
+  {
+    std::getline(state, allm);
+    std::getline(state, modeId);
+    state >> modeRate;
+  }
+
+  const std::string vrrMode =
+      CSysfsPath("/sys/class/amhdmitx/amhdmitx0/vrr_mode").Get<std::string>().value_or("");
+  const std::string mode = m_amlDRMUtils->aml_get_drmDevice_mode();
+  const bool onFs3dMode = StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(mode, FS3D_MODE) ||
+                          StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(mode, FS3D_MODE_165);
+  // left by a Kodi in 3D; the base mode alone is also a desktop someone chose
+  const bool left = saved || StringUtils::StartsWith(vrrMode, "game") ||
+                    CSysfsPath(FS3D_SWAP).Get<int>().value_or(0) != 0;
+
+  // Nothing plays yet: the video layer starts in 2D whatever is found. The
+  // kernel keeps the 3D type across a decoder reset (a pause or a seek needs it
+  // kept), so it is not cleared for us when a Kodi dies.
+  aml_set_3d_video_mode(0 /* MODE_3D_DISABLE */, false, 3);
+  CSysfsPath(FS3D_SWAP, 0);
+
+  if (!left && !onFs3dMode)
+    return;
+
+  CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "CAMLDisplay::{} - taking down frame-sequential 3D left by a previous run "
+            "(saved {}, vrr {}, mode {})", __FUNCTION__, saved, vrrMode, mode);
+  // ALLM goes back to what it was before 3D; without that record, ALLM on next
+  // to the rest of 3D was ours
+  if (left)
+    m_fs3d_allm = saved ? StringUtils::Trim(allm) : std::string("0");
+  else
+    m_fs3d_allm = CSysfsPath(FS3D_ALLM).Get<std::string>().value_or("0");
+  fs3d_apply(false, 0);
+
+  // Kodi takes its desktop from the mode the output is on: not the 3D base, or
+  // it keeps it, and the box boots at it, from now on. The record stays until
+  // the output has been switched off the base mode.
+  if (onFs3dMode && left)
   {
-    fs3d_apply(false, 0);
-    aml_set_3d_video_mode(0 /* MODE_3D_DISABLE */, false, 3);
-    CSysfsPath(FS3D_SWAP, 0);
+    m_fs3d_recovered_desktop = std::make_pair(modeId, modeRate);
+    m_fs3d_state_pending = saved;
   }
+  else
+    fs3d_state_clear();
 }
 
 // Without HDMI 3D the only stereo output is HFR VRR. Taking stereo video as
@@ -1218,6 +1290,11 @@ bool CAMLDisplay::set_native_resolution(const RESOLUTION_INFO &res, std::string
       handle_display_stereo_mode(stereo_mode);
   }
 
+  // a recovered desktop is set: the record of the 3D left behind can go
+  if (result && !StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(res.strId, FS3D_MODE) &&
+      !StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(res.strId, FS3D_MODE_165) && m_fs3d_state_pending.exchange(false))
+    fs3d_state_clear();
+
   return result;
 }
 
@@ -1282,7 +1359,13 @@ bool CAMLDisplay::set_fs3d_resolution(const RESOLUTION_INFO &res, std::string fr
     m_fs3d_vrr_frac = false;
     m_fs3d_vsync_hz = 0.0;
     CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "CAMLDisplay::{} - left frame-sequential 3D", __FUNCTION__);
-    return set_display_resolution(res, framebuffer_name, true, hotplug_mode_switch);
+    // the record goes once the output is off the 3D base mode, not before
+    const bool restored = set_display_resolution(res, framebuffer_name, true, hotplug_mode_switch);
+    if (restored)
+      fs3d_state_clear();
+    else
+      m_fs3d_state_pending = true;
+    return restored;
   }
 
   // The film rate: the video's own, or the refresh Kodi picked for it.
@@ -1308,6 +1391,14 @@ bool CAMLDisplay::set_fs3d_resolution(const RESOLUTION_INFO &res, std::string fr
   {
     m_fs3d_allm = CSysfsPath(FS3D_ALLM).Get<std::string>().value_or("0");
     StringUtils::Trim(m_fs3d_allm);
+    RESOLUTION_INFO before;
+    // Already on the base mode (a switch back failed, or a recovery is under
+    // way): a record there names the desktop, and is kept.
+    const bool known = aml_get_native_resolution(&before);
+    const bool onBase = StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(before.strId, FS3D_MODE) ||
+                        StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(before.strId, FS3D_MODE_165);
+    if (known && !(onBase && std::ifstream(CSpecialProtocol::TranslatePath(FS3D_STATE)).good()))
+      fs3d_state_save(m_fs3d_allm, before);
   }
   const bool switch_mode = force_mode_switch || !m_fs3d_active || twin;
   if (!set_display_resolution(base, framebuffer_name, switch_mode, hotplug_mode_switch))
@@ -1329,7 +1420,12 @@ bool CAMLDisplay::set_fs3d_resolution(const RESOLUTION_INFO &res, std::string fr
     m_fs3d_vsync_hz = 0.0;
     // for the rest of this film: it is not held back waiting for it
     m_fs3d_entry_failed = true;
-    return set_display_resolution(res, framebuffer_name, true, hotplug_mode_switch);
+    const bool restored = set_display_resolution(res, framebuffer_name, true, hotplug_mode_switch);
+    if (restored)
+      fs3d_state_clear();
+    else
+      m_fs3d_state_pending = true;
+    return restored;
   }
 
   const int vrr_rate = rates.vrrRate;
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/AMLDisplay.h b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/AMLDisplay.h
index dc9fee6cac..b80c7b28f0 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/AMLDisplay.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/AMLDisplay.h
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@
 #include <xf86drmMode.h>
 #include <atomic>
 #include <memory>
+#include <optional>
+#include <string>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <utility>
 #include <vector>
@@ -233,6 +235,12 @@ public:
   void aml_fs3d_playback_stopped() { m_fs3d_entry_failed = false; }
   //! a decoder closed: in frame-sequential 3D, the next film of a playlist may follow
   void aml_fs3d_decoder_closed();
+  //! The mode (name, rate) the output was on before a previous Kodi entered 3D
+  //! and died in it, once: the desktop, not the 3D base mode it was left on.
+  std::optional<std::pair<std::string, float>> aml_fs3d_take_recovered_desktop()
+  {
+    return std::exchange(m_fs3d_recovered_desktop, std::nullopt);
+  }
 private:
   bool set_fs3d_resolution(const RESOLUTION_INFO &res, std::string framebuffer_name,
     const RenderStereoMode stereo_mode, bool force_mode_switch, bool hotplug_mode_switch);
@@ -247,6 +255,9 @@ private:
     bool operator==(const Fs3dRates&) const = default;
   };
   Fs3dRates fs3d_rates(float fps) const;
+  void fs3d_state_save(const std::string& allm, const RESOLUTION_INFO& before);
+  void fs3d_state_clear();
+  void fs3d_recover();
   static constexpr const char* FS3D_OSD = "/sys/module/aml_drm/parameters/osd_fa_3d";
   static constexpr const char* FS3D_VRR_RATE = "/sys/class/amhdmitx/amhdmitx0/vrr_rate";
   static constexpr const char* FS3D_ALLM = "/sys/class/amhdmitx/amhdmitx0/allm_mode";
@@ -280,4 +291,7 @@ private:
   std::string m_fs3d_165_failed;
   //! a refresh read frame-sequential 3D as gone and it was kept: the next one decides
   bool m_fs3d_drop_seen = false;
+  std::optional<std::pair<std::string, float>> m_fs3d_recovered_desktop;
+  //! the record of a 3D left behind is kept until its desktop has been set
+  std::atomic<bool> m_fs3d_state_pending{false};
 };
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp
index 81402af1a9..7f986c9b01 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp
@@ -623,6 +623,61 @@ void CWinSystemAmlogic::RefreshResolutions()
   if (m_amlDisplay->aml_get_native_resolution(&curDisplay))
     resDesktop = curDisplay;
 
+  // left on the 3D base mode by a Kodi that died in 3D: the desktop is the mode before it
+  if (const auto before = m_amlDisplay->aml_fs3d_take_recovered_desktop())
+  {
+    for (const auto& res : resolutions)
+    {
+      if (StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(res.strId, before->first) &&
+          std::fabs(res.fRefreshRate - before->second) < 0.01f)
+      {
+        CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "{}: desktop {} at {:.3f} Hz, as before 3D", __FUNCTION__, res.strId,
+                  res.fRefreshRate);
+        resDesktop = res;
+        break;
+      }
+    }
+    // Not listed any more (another sink): the sink's preferred mode, else the
+    // nearest mode of the current size that is not a 3D base, so the output
+    // leaves the base and the record of the 3D left behind can go.
+    if (!StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(resDesktop.strId, before->first))
+    {
+      const auto isBase = [](const std::string& id) {
+        return StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(id, CAMLDisplay::FS3D_MODE) ||
+               StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(id, CAMLDisplay::FS3D_MODE_165);
+      };
+      const std::string preferred = m_amlDisplay->aml_get_preferred_mode();
+      std::optional<RESOLUTION_INFO> desktop;
+      for (const auto& res : resolutions)
+      {
+        if (isBase(res.strId))
+          continue;
+        if (StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(res.strId, preferred))
+        {
+          desktop = res;
+          break;
+        }
+        if (res.iScreenWidth == curDisplay.iScreenWidth &&
+            res.iScreenHeight == curDisplay.iScreenHeight &&
+            (res.dwFlags & D3DPRESENTFLAG_MODEMASK) ==
+                (curDisplay.dwFlags & D3DPRESENTFLAG_MODEMASK) &&
+            (!desktop || std::fabs(res.fRefreshRate - curDisplay.fRefreshRate) <
+                             std::fabs(desktop->fRefreshRate - curDisplay.fRefreshRate)))
+          desktop = res;
+      }
+      if (desktop)
+      {
+        CLog::Log(LOGWARNING, "{}: {} from before 3D is not listed, desktop {} at {:.3f} Hz",
+                  __FUNCTION__, before->first, desktop->strId, desktop->fRefreshRate);
+        resDesktop = *desktop;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
+  bool desktopFound = false;
+  std::optional<RESOLUTION_INFO> desktopTwin;
+  std::optional<RESOLUTION_INFO> desktopNearest;
+
   for (auto& res : resolutions)
   {
     CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "Found resolution {:d} x {:d} with {:d} x {:d}{} @ {:f} Hz",
@@ -642,12 +697,48 @@ void CWinSystemAmlogic::RefreshResolutions()
        resDesktop.iHeight == res.iHeight &&
        resDesktop.iScreenWidth == res.iScreenWidth &&
        resDesktop.iScreenHeight == res.iScreenHeight &&
-       (resDesktop.dwFlags & D3DPRESENTFLAG_MODEMASK) == (res.dwFlags & D3DPRESENTFLAG_MODEMASK) &&
-       fabs(resDesktop.fRefreshRate - res.fRefreshRate) < FLT_EPSILON)
+       (resDesktop.dwFlags & D3DPRESENTFLAG_MODEMASK) == (res.dwFlags & D3DPRESENTFLAG_MODEMASK))
+    {
+      if (fabs(resDesktop.fRefreshRate - res.fRefreshRate) < FLT_EPSILON)
+      {
+        // update desktop resolution
+        CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetResolutionInfo(RES_DESKTOP) = res;
+        desktopFound = true;
+      }
+      else if (!desktopTwin &&
+               std::lround(resDesktop.fRefreshRate) == std::lround(res.fRefreshRate))
+        desktopTwin = res;
+      if (!desktopNearest || std::fabs(res.fRefreshRate - resDesktop.fRefreshRate) <
+                                 std::fabs(desktopNearest->fRefreshRate - resDesktop.fRefreshRate))
+        desktopNearest = res;
+    }
+  }
+
+  // A current mode the list has no entry for (119.88, or 1080p165 whose VESA timing
+  // is not listed, left by a Kodi that died in frame-sequential 3D) takes its listed
+  // twin, else the same size at the nearest rate, else the sink's preferred mode or
+  // the first listed: with no desktop mode the window is never created.
+  if (!desktopFound && !resolutions.empty())
+  {
+    std::optional<RESOLUTION_INFO> desktop = desktopTwin ? desktopTwin : desktopNearest;
+    if (!desktop)
     {
-      // update desktop resolution
-      CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetResolutionInfo(RES_DESKTOP) = res;
+      const std::string preferred = m_amlDisplay->aml_get_preferred_mode();
+      for (const auto& res : resolutions)
+      {
+        if (StringUtils::EqualsNoCase(res.strId, preferred))
+        {
+          desktop = res;
+          break;
+        }
+      }
+      if (!desktop)
+        desktop = resolutions.front();
     }
+    CLog::Log(LOGWARNING, "{}: current mode {} at {:.3f} Hz is not listed, using {} at {:.3f} Hz",
+              __FUNCTION__, resDesktop.strId, resDesktop.fRefreshRate, desktop->strId,
+              desktop->fRefreshRate);
+    CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetResolutionInfo(RES_DESKTOP) = *desktop;
   }
 }
 
